  Version 0.1.3 (2026-11-07)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Korean LOCAL4 after the second-model review (ORDER 447; gpt-6.1-sol through the Codex CLI, answer accepted by Opus as written):
    the Korean line omitted what FILE is, which the English and the other languages say. It now ends with
    "(파일은 해당 파일의 경로입니다)." The other eight languages were reviewed OK and are unchanged. Still a first
    draft with AI assistance, pending review by native speakers. The tests now check the Korean message.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.2 (2026-11-07)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * LOCAL4 after ORDER 440's review (gpt-6.1-sol through the Codex CLI, accepted by Opus): the Korean command line is
    "다음 명령을 실행하세요: wine start /unix 파일" without the malformed space before 을(를); the English says what FILE
    is ("FILE is the path of the file") and "exit status"; the other seven languages follow the English, with FILE
    translated where the language already did. Still a first draft with AI assistance, pending review by native speakers.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.1 (2026-11-06)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * A file Wine cannot start is no longer silent (ORDER 437, memory no-silent-fallbacks): the worker reads each Wine
    process's status, tells the person which file failed and with what status in their language (kdialog, or the
    terminal when there is none), and exits 1. LOCAL4 in the nine languages, a first draft with AI assistance, pending
    review by native speakers.

